net/sched: sch_cake: cake_mq tin_cap on top of per-tin share

With 999-715 (tin_share = 1), a limited tin served by several cake_mq
instances gets its aggregate threshold divided per instance. A priority
tin concentrated on one instance can then hold that instance's whole
share (in diffserv4, Voice = rate/4 equals the instance rate with four
active instances), so a large priority-marked flow starves the lower
tins sharing that instance. Segalmen reports this directly: a ping in
the Video tin sharing the queue of an 800 Mbit/s CS4 flow sees 105-114
ms max, versus < 4 ms for the same flow left unmarked.

Add a runtime knob, off by default (debugfs cake_mq/tin_cap):

  0     = unchanged (999-715 behaviour)
  1-100 = with tin_share, the threshold of a limited tin (threshold
          below the full rate) never exceeds tin_cap % of this
          instance's rate. The full-rate (best effort) tin is left
          alone.

The cap is applied after the per-tin division, so it bounds the
per-instance threshold rather than the aggregate one, and only ever
lowers it. Out of tin_share, the knob has no effect.

Counters: the cake_mq/stats lines get a "tin_capped" row per direction
(number of syncs where the cap was applied, per tin); the rows before
it are unchanged, so existing parsers keep working.

tin_capped is incremented once per sync tick, by the tick winner alone,
to match Segalmen's counter (his sync body runs once per tick; ours runs
per instance). The winner is the one instance that took
cfg->sync_lock and saw a full tick elapse; it is marked by a stack-local
won_tick flag, so no extra lock is added. capped_mask is identical on
every instance (same cap, same global thresholds, same published
tin_active vector), so counting on the winner gives exactly one
increment per tick and the mask stays exact.

Ports Segalmen's patch 729 (github.com/Segalmen/cake-mq-patches), and
depends on patch 720 (per-tin active share) via our 999-715, onto our
shared-shaper series (999-711..715): his tin_others / last_checked
become our shared_tin_active / shared_last_checked, and the counters
land in our stats struct.

Source: Segalmen/cake-mq-patches, patches 720 (cake_mq per-tin active
share) and 729 (tin_cap on top of per-tin share), commit
977388f114daf427145f4f6845df7b82b1b34fec, GPL-2.0.

Not built, not flashed.

